  "hold_reasons": [
    "FSSAI FSSR ghee identity does not by itself prove each broad CTR 'Milk and Milk products' pesticide entry applies to clarified milk-fat ingredient.",
    "Carbendazim's (F) qualifier is explicitly defined in the CTR footnote as MRL calculated on fat basis; do not use it as ordinary milk-mass unit.",
    "Carbofuran requires parent plus 3-hydroxy-carbofuran sum expressed as carbofuran, using fat-basis comparison; a parent-only laboratory result is insufficient.",
    "Raw ingredient origin, species, ghee grade, actual analytical extraction method, concentration/processing factors and product formula remain unverified.",
    "Official FSSR 2.1.8 source text was checked but page-image confirmation and all updated Gazette amendments were not independently completed in this pass.",
    "Recipe 14.6 retains official source title/method alignment hold; no claimed source reference can override this block.",
    "These are two selected reference rows, not the entire pesticide, heavy-metal, antibiotic, mycotoxin or microbial requirement panel.",
    "The generic edible-fat/vegetable-oil metal and pesticide rows are NOT automatically inherited by ghee.",
    "Future 1 December 2026 contaminant amendment is NOT treated as effective on 4 November 2026."
  ],
